A postdoctoral fellow position is available in the department of Bioinformatics & Computational Biology. The postdoctoral fellow will develop computational (machine-learning) methods, and biologically meaningful models; perform statistical analyses to interpret large-scale genomics/clinical data, especially single-cell and spatial omics data, towards understanding cancer etiology, evolution, and response to therapies. The department of Bioinformatics and Computational Biology focuses on developing and delivering cutting-edge data science to cancer research and medical applications. 
 All duties and responsibilities are carried out in compliance with institutional policies, ethical research standards, and applicable federal and state regulations. 
 LEARNING OBJECTIVES 
 Achieve scholarly impact; 
 Define career path; 
 Publish high impact publications; 
 Gain experience leading projects,

